#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:5 a9796ff165db406c86e9bba0182ac4ee
msgid "Booster Motor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:10 6bb98f83e4d34e73a8490239f755428c
msgid ""
"Copter 3.6 (and higher) and QuadPlanes support additional motors placed "
"in the middle of the frame to provide additional lift.  This feature is "
"compatible with any of the multicopter frame types (i.e. quad, tri, hexa,"
" octa, dodecahexa).  The video above shows this feature used along with "
"an :ref:`internal combustion engine <common-ice>` but the feature can "
"also be used with electric motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:14 a0ebac4885904e49ad5e2ed519e9f99e
msgid ""
"Copter does not yet support horizontally facing motors to provide "
"movement without leaning the vehicle (`enhancement request is here "
"<https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/issues/10117>`__)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:17 1496e46eafa64eb2928300785af7bd14
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:19 f5ceb8f17fca4c00b12de115247708c7
msgid ""
"Connect the booster motor's ESCs to one of the autopilot's RC Output "
"ports (i.e. MAIN OUT 1 ~ 8 or AUX OUT 1 ~ 6)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:20 65bdc9d149a24a8481e9b527741cb788
msgid ""
"Set SERVOx_FUNCTION = 81 for \"Boost Throttle\" (where \"x\" is the servo"
" output number)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/booster-motor.rst:21 c553507e344b43179767e8fea2ddbb46
msgid ""
"Optionally set :ref:`MOT_BOOST_SCALE <MOT_BOOST_SCALE>` to a value "
"between 0 to 5 to scale the output for the booster based on the average "
"output throttle sent to the standard motors.  A higher scaling factor "
"will put more of the load on the booster motor.  1 will set the "
"BoostThrottle equal to the main throttle.  The output to the main motor "
"will always be between the ``SERVOx_MIN`` and ``SERVOx_MAX`` values "
"(where \"x\" is the servo output number)"
msgstr ""

